  "slug": "tally-financial-year-voucher-filter",
  "title": "Finding Tally Vouchers Near the Financial-Year Boundary",
  "description": "Use a March and April example to see how the accounting period and date filters affect voucher searches.",
  "category": "Vouchers and Day Book",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Identify the date on the voucher",
      "body": "Read the date inside TallyPrime before you search. In an illustrative April-to-March year, a sale dated 31 March and a receipt dated 1 April sit on opposite sides of the boundary. The dates control the lookup even if the same customer appears in both."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Set the period before searching",
      "body": "Select the financial year that contains the transaction, then select a date range within that period. Search for the type and number only after setting those filters. For the example, look in the ending year for the sale and the next year for the receipt."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Use one voucher to confirm the fix",
      "body": "If you find the entry after switching the filter, compare the party and amount with TallyPrime. If it still cannot be found under the right company and date, check the latest sync. Give support the exact voucher date and the ranges you tried."
    }
  ],
